WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
The ROWS frame counts ordered rows.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:06.117
Two preceding means up to two earlier rows.

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:13.402
It does not mean two days, two hours, or two months unless every time unit has exactly one

00:00:13.402 --> 00:00:17.062
row. This distinction matters when the sequence has gaps.

00:00:17.062 --> 00:00:22.522
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:27.732
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:31.267
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:36.160
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
